// One rounding everywhere: round(x, places, mode), number_format and format("{:.Nf}") agree, an int or decimal
// rounds exactly and a real rounds as the decimal it prints as. The table is Python's decimal module (quantize,
// ROUND_HALF_UP / HALF_EVEN / HALF_DOWN / UP / DOWN / FLOOR / CEILING), made once and written here; the one place
// grain differs on purpose is a zero: never -0.00.
